{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["For you have striven — from the root און, 'to strive with Elohim,' like קנה קנית, עשה עשית. But וישר אל מלאך ויוכל is from the root שב קם רץ, so that it would be said ויקם וישר וירץ. And the reason Yaakov was struck and limped: because the Holy One, blessed be He, had promised him, yet he was fleeing. And so we find in all who travel a path not in accordance with the will of the Holy One, blessed be He, or who refuse to go — they were punished. Of Moshe it is written: שלח נא ביד תשלח ויחר אף ה׳ במשה. And according to the derash — even though the Sages said that in every case חרון אף leaves a mark, here what mark is there? Behold, Aharon your brother the Levite is destined to become a Levite while you are a priest, and now he will become a priest while you become a Levite. But according to the peshat: because he was reluctant to go, it is written: ויהי בדרך במלון ויפגשהו ה׳ ויבקש המיתו. And so with Yonah, who was swallowed in the belly of the fish. And so with Bilaam: ויחר אף אלהים כי הולך הוא, and he was made lame, as it is written: ותלחץ רגל בלעם. And וילך שפי 'lame,' like ושפו עצמותיו."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The lemma כי שרית is Rashbam's paraphrase of כי שרית עם אלהים (v. 29). The phrase או ממאנים ללכת is rendered literally; it may carry a textual difficulty."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:09.270835486Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}